  <ym-title|Scalar price and receipt audit><label|scalar-price-and-receipt-audit>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected finite-volume nonlinear step.

    <item>Status: draft; local mathematical and source-correspondence review
    pending.

    <item>Imported source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Prose: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/rg-price-receipts.tex>.

    <item>Scope: proves the eventual numerical Tariff inequalities and
    records the exact public selected-run supplier path for shipment, arrival
    allowances/gains, and reset-rate payments. It does not reprove the
    imported analytic rate producers or the full selected schedule.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Scalar tariff crosswalk><label|scalar-tariff-crosswalk>

  The source target parameters are denoted here by relative weight
  <verbatim|lambda>, target exponent <verbatim|rho>, strength <verbatim|mu>,
  and fixed <verbatim|C = Footprint.preCost(Q.halo+5)>. The manuscript's
  <verbatim|b(x)> is <verbatim|betaF G x L = x + G.slopeConstant * log
  L.val>; <verbatim|R(x)> is <verbatim|radiusB x = Nat.ceil((log x)^2)>; and
  <verbatim|M(x)> is <verbatim|Vac.Numbers.P (b(x)) = exp((log(log
  b(x)))^2)>. Its site factor is <verbatim|e*(2*(16*r+9))^4>.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  term or conclusion>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified source and
  path>>|<cell|<strong|Checked correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|station(x)=x^(-1)>,
  <verbatim|probe(x)=x^(-2)>, <verbatim|radiusTab(r,N,a)=(N*siteFactor(r)+4)*a>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.station>,
  <verbatim|.probe>, <verbatim|.radiusTab>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Revenue.lean>>|<cell|These give <verbatim|f>,
  <verbatim|y>, and <verbatim|k>.>>|<row|<cell|Actual tail cost
  <verbatim|straw(mu,L,G,x)+N*siteFactor(radiusB x)*probe(betaF G x
  L)>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.thaws>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.straw>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.lauge>;
  <verbatim|YM.Push.AbsoluteSums.Delay.fineMonitor>;
  <verbatim|YM.Vac.Numbers.P>; paths <verbatim|MergeProof/Revenue.lean>,
  <verbatim|PhysicalNext/.../Mallow/Stove.lean>,
  <verbatim|Push/ABSOLUTE_SUMS/Delay.lean>,
  <verbatim|Vac/Treasury.lean>>|<cell|Exactly the manuscript's <verbatim|z>:
  <verbatim|straw=2 exp(-mu*M^2/16)>, since <verbatim|fineMonitor(x)=P(betaF
  G x L)>.>>|<row|<cell|Radius and site-factor
  rates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Rate.radius_price>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Tariff.warmLane>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.E09.radiusB_shift>; paths
  <verbatim|AnalyticNext/CONNECTED_ACTIVITY_JETS_E6/Numerics.lean>,
  <verbatim|MergeProof/Revenue.lean>, <verbatim|Work/E09/Scales.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|radiusB(x)>
  and its fixed polynomials have rate zero; <verbatim|radiusB(betaF G x L)
  \<less\>= 2*radiusB(x)> eventually by <verbatim|YM.Push.AbsoluteSums.Fees.horizons>,
  applied in <verbatim|Tariff.thaws> with <verbatim|2*Q.\<varepsilon\>
  \<less\> P.top.supportExponent>. The manuscript proves the fixed-shift
  radius comparison directly.>>|<row|<cell|Tail rate <verbatim|-2>, purchase
  margin, lodging, and credit>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.infuso>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.thaws>; paths
  <verbatim|PhysicalNext/.../Mallow/Stove.lean>,
  <verbatim|MergeProof/Revenue.lean>>|<cell|Imported Gaussian rate is
  <verbatim|Rate -2>; manuscript reorganizes the rate algebra and proves the
  eventual scalar inequalities explicitly.>>|<row|<cell|Shipment
  bound>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Merge.Palette.shipPrice>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Permit.lean>);
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Tariff.thaws>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Revenue.lean>);
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Daisy.ribbon>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/Daisy/Solvent.lean>)>|<cell|Source
  inequality is <verbatim|N*siteFactor(radiusB x)*exp((Q.relative+1)*C)*a
  \<less\>= Q.goal(L,x)*exp(Q.relative*C)>. With <verbatim|a=station(betaF G
  x L)>, <verbatim|Q.relative=lambda>, <verbatim|Q.rate=rho>, and
  <verbatim|Q.goal=b^rho>, this is the displayed shipping inequality.
  <verbatim|Tariff.thaws> derives the <verbatim|-1> rate for the left side
  after division by <verbatim|exp(Q.relative*C)>, then spends the strict gap
  <verbatim|Q.rate \<gtr\> -1> using <verbatim|Q.start>.>>>>>

  The new scalar proof is reorganized mathematics, not a literal translation
  of <verbatim|Tariff.thaws>; it spells out fixed-shift logarithmic radii,
  rate arithmetic, and strict-exponent spending. The equality for the straw
  cost and the source formula for each tariff field were checked directly.

  <section|Exact public receipt chain and <verbatim|hS>/<verbatim|hF>
  roles><label|exact-public-receipt-chain-and-hshf-roles>

  The selected construction does not treat the three receipts as one
  hypothesis.

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.resoling>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Leaping.lean>, first obtains an arena using
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.yearEnd>, then applies
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.brevity> to obtain
    <verbatim|Arrives> on a common enlarged delay. It subsequently refines
    that delay using <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Graces.reacts>,
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Circlet.chords>, the selected
    menu, <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Graces.compass>, and
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Cub.motions>, and calls
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.scarce> to obtain
    <verbatim|Minty>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Arrives> is the source
    object called <verbatim|hS> at local <verbatim|Many.ripe>/<verbatim|Photo.bidding>
    interfaces. Its first clause is the amnesty/activity witness. Its first
    payment clause is: for <verbatim|c,k \<gtr\>= 0>, <verbatim|k \<less\>=
    b^(-1/8)>, and <verbatim|c \<less\>= exp(-mark(x))>, there is a
    rate-payment witness at spatial scale <verbatim|radiusB(x)> with rates
    <verbatim|stems> for <verbatim|c,k>. Its second clause concerns
    <verbatim|softNeed> at a reset-compatible profile;
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.offerS> bounds that request by
    <verbatim|b^(-1/4)>, and <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.mingle>
    pays it at the <verbatim|straw>/<verbatim|stems> scales.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Pungent>, the source object
    called <verbatim|hF> at <verbatim|Many.crowd2>, is supplied as the hold
    field of <verbatim|Minty> by <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Tray.bravo>
    and <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.scarce>. It has the same
    marked payment but with the larger cap
    <verbatim|exp(Trio.coverTicket(halo))*b^(-1/8)>. Its reset clause is for
    the opened request <verbatim|Spicy.opens>, using the base profile's clip,
    width, and paths and <verbatim|Time.credit(profile)*deltaE(x)>; it
    requires the same reset-size constraint and yields a rate-payment witness
    at <verbatim|straw>/<verbatim|stems>. In <verbatim|Tray.bravo>,
    <verbatim|offerSp> and <verbatim|mingle> produce these clauses;
    <verbatim|Groom.scarce> combines them with the separate Tariff receipt on
    a common delay.

    <item>The Tariff receipt is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Rumor>,
    supplied by <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Tariff.thaws> and
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.scarce>. It is distinct from both
    <verbatim|Arrives> and <verbatim|Pungent>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.paneer>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Wax.lean>, passes the <verbatim|.probeT>,
    <verbatim|.small>, <verbatim|.buy>, <verbatim|.lodging>, and
    <verbatim|.credits> Tariff fields and the shipment field to
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Many.ripe>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tanger.lean>. The latter calls
    <verbatim|Photo.bidding>, <verbatim|Many.usable>, <verbatim|Many.crowd2>,
    and <verbatim|Photo.shade>. The public selected-run route reaches this
    through <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.resoling>;
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.fiscaler> closes the resulting
    run-level quantifiers.
  </enumerate>

  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Daisy.stables> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/Daisy/Corral.lean>
  is the actual eventual producer of the <verbatim|Bikes> allow/gains record
  and its tail-cost bound. It uses <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Daisy.scaleHome>,
  <verbatim|.strides>, <verbatim|.burden>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Daisy.sailsW>,
  <verbatim|YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Target.rate_none>,
  <verbatim|YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Target.rate_root>, the radius/horizon
  comparison, and rate decay. The record states, in particular,
  <verbatim|0\<less\>e>, <verbatim|v+e+e\<less\>=Q.exp>,
  <verbatim|degreePrice(radiusB x,pledgeA,e)\<less\>=sailUp>,
  <verbatim|degreePrice(radiusB x,pledgeQ,e)\<less\>=1/2>,
  <verbatim|sailUp\<less\>=1/2>, and <verbatim|pledgeQ\<less\>=1/2> as its
  separate gain field; these are then the hypotheses used by
  <verbatim|amnesty>/<verbatim|Arrives>. The present manuscript proves the
  Tariff arithmetic but does not reproduce the full source proof of
  <verbatim|stables>, <verbatim|amnesty>, <verbatim|Arena>, or the schedule
  construction. These remain imported source producers and are not being
  claimed as consequences of the scalar proposition.

  <section|Commands and review limits><label|commands-and-review-limits>

  Read-only source inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on
  the files named above, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/E09/Scales.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/{Mallow/Eco.lean,Daisy/Corral.lean}>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/{Revenue.lean,Tray.lean,Groom.lean,Wax.lean,Tanger.lean,Leaping.lean}>,
  and <verbatim|source/upstream.json>; <verbatim|git status --short>
  confirmed only draft paths were untracked. No Lean build, LaTeX build, or
  blueprint checker has been run for this addition. The proof unit metadata
  and integration are owned by the parent.

